<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.12.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00260</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.12.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>c138de0a-da03-47f6-8bc9-983bc7032453</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will continue to examine and create linear models with linear equations relating two variables. You will also look at several ways to write the equation of a line based on the information given.When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Write an equation of the line given the slope and \( y \)-intercept.</item>
        <item>Write an equation of the line given the slope and a point.</item>
        <item>Write an equation of the line given two points.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00002">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>1.12.1: Using the Slope Formula</item>
        <item>1.12.2: Writing an Equation Given the Slope and \(y\)-Intercept<list id="list-00003">
            <item>1.12.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.12.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>1.12.3: Writing an Equation Given the Slope and a Point<list id="list-00004">
            <item>1.12.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.12.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>1.12.4: Writing Equations in Different Forms <list id="list-00005">
            <item>1.12.4: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.12.4: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>1.12.5: Writing an Equation Given Two Points <list id="list-00006">
            <item>1.12.5: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.12.5: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>1.12.6: Choosing a Method to Write an Equation</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00007">
        <item>1.12.7: Practice</item>
        <item>1.12.8: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>